## Evidence rules
Every observation MUST include at least one evidence object whose chat_id/turn_id (or Brain source) appears in the supplied source text. Copy IDs exactly. Do not invent IDs.
- Turn evidence requires chat_id and turn_id from the batch.
- Brain evidence uses source_kind "brain" and MUST omit chat_id and turn_id.
- Quotes must be short and copied from the source.
- Prefer the strongest direct user quote over an assistant paraphrase. If the user accepts earlier AI advice, include the user's acceptance evidence.
- One explicit user statement can be sufficient. Repeated inferred preferences need multiple independent user interactions and must remain uncertain with moderate confidence.

## Output
Return JSON only:
{
  "observations": [
    {
      "category": "decision",
      "subject": "short subject",
      "observation": "one concise independently useful sentence",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chat_id": "...",
          "turn_id": "...",
          "source_kind": "user_message",
          "epistemic_role": "user_confirmed",
          "quote": "short quote"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "warnings": []
}

Confidence must be a number from 0.0 to 1.0.
